+# Dobe Sheets private transport
+
+The opt-in `dobe` feature builds `dobe-sheets`, a file-only entry point. It does not start the editor, upstream MCP server, script interpreter, macro runner, Python runner or external-link resolver. The ordinary upstream entry point is unchanged.
+
+The first supported profile, `cells-and-formulas-v1`, uses the complete native Workbook JSON model, including its native style table and sparse cell storage. Inputs must match native serialization exactly at the JSON-value level. Unknown fields, omitted defaults, malformed cell storage, unsupported workbook features and invalid style references fail rather than being repaired or discarded. Output files must not exist. JSON transport does not promise XLSX preservation or Office round-trip compatibility.
+
+Commands:
+
+- `new OUTPUT` writes the complete native default workbook.
+- `encode INPUT OUTPUT` validates and cold-reopens a complete workbook without recalculating it.
+- `recalc INPUT OUTPUT` uses the native dependency and calculation engine. Only cached formula values may change.
+- `edit INPUT REQUEST OUTPUT` applies a JSON array of cell changes, recalculates, validates and saves. Each change requires zero-based `sheet` and A1 `cell`; `value` (null, boolean, finite number or text) and `formula` are mutually exclusive. Optional `format` supports `bold`, `italic` and `number_format`. A failed batch creates no output.
+- `export csv|html INPUT OUTPUT` exports the active sheet through the native exporter. It checks all cached formula values against a fresh calculation first and refuses stale caches. CSV is a values export; the native workbook retains formulas and formatting. HTML is a structural, styled preview with browser-dependent fonts; it is not a pinned-font raster fidelity claim.
+
+Limits: 8 MiB JSON, 200,000 JSON nodes, 1–8 sheets, 10,000 occupied cells, 512 rows by 64 columns per sheet, 256 styles, 1,024 formulas and 1,000,000 total referenced cells across formula trees. Formula text is at most 2,048 bytes, 128 AST nodes, depth 32; a range has at most 4,096 cells. Edits contain 1–1,024 operations. Text cells support Unicode up to 16,384 UTF-8 bytes.
+
+Supported formulas are scalar arithmetic/comparison, unary plus/minus/percent, same-sheet or named-sheet cell references, and SUM, AVERAGE, MIN, MAX, COUNT, COUNTA, IF, IFERROR, ROUND and ABS. Bounded ranges are admitted only as aggregate arguments. Constants and native error results are retained. Dynamic arrays, Python, macros, external workbooks, defined names, volatile functions, concatenation, whole-column/row references and other expressions are refused. Number formats are General, 0, 0.00, #,##0, #,##0.00, 0% and 0.00%. Other workbook and sheet state must equal native defaults, except sheet names, active sheet, cells and the admitted styles.
+
+This private engine is not public runtime registration or distribution qualification. Durable jobs, portable project history, installed execution, Linux evidence and full release gates must be qualified separately. No editor window or remote operation is needed to build or exercise this transport.
